  "mn54:0.2": "<p><i>In this passage, the Buddha teaches Potaliya the householder what it means, in the discipline of a noble one, to have entirely cut off one’s worldly affairs.</i></p><p>See also: <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn13'>MN 13</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn14'>MN 14</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn22'>MN 22</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn82'>MN 82</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an5.76'>AN 5:76</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an7.74'>AN 7:70</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp146-156#dhp146'>Dhp 146–156</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/snp4.1'>Sn 4:1</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thig13.1'>Thig 13:1</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thig13.5'>Thig 13:5</a>; <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thig14.1'>Thig 14</a></p>",
